==English==
{{wikipedia|Styx (mythology)}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|Στύξ|lit=Hate|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/stɪks/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/stIks/}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|sticks}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{context|Greek mythology|lang=en}} 
## One of the [[rivers]] in [[Hades]], over which the [[soul]]s of the dead are [[ferried]] across by [[Charon]].  The gods also swore unbreakable swore oaths upon the river Styx.  
## The [[goddess]] of the [[river]] Styx, in Hades.  She is the [[wife]] of the [[Titan]], [[Pallas]], and the [[mother]] of [[Nike]] (Victory), [[Kratos]] (Strength), [[Bia]] (Force), and [[Zelus]] (Zeal).  

====Coordinate terms====
* {{sense|Rivers in Hades}} [[Acheron]] (Woe; Distress), [[Alpheus]] (Whitish), [[Cocytus]] (Lamentation, Wailing), [[Eridanos]] (Amber), [[Lethe]] (Oblivion, Forgetfulness, Unmindfulness), [[Phlegethon]] (Flaming, Fire).

